00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.35 to +1.07) and highs show no clear change. The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 1 of 12 months; April fell. Highs rose in 9 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Valentine's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.14 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 20.8 inches a year. The wettest year was 1977 (32.68 in); the driest, 1894 (10.14 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 9 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}